{"name":"Locks of Love style hair donation","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Donation_hair_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Donation_hair_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donation_hair_(cropped).jpg","caption":"Donation hair (cropped)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Hair donation means growing hair out and cutting it for a charity that makes wigs for children with hair loss. For the donor, the appeal is a style reset: a long-hair phase, then a cut into a shorter look.","Locks of Love, founded in 1997, popularised the practice in the United States. It requires donated hair to be at least 10 inches long."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People grow hair to the required length, tie it in ponytails or braids, have it cut by a stylist, and send it to the charity. Many then keep a shorter style."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Few physical risks. Donors should know the length rules and that much donated hair is sold rather than used in wigs, per the charity."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Donation_hair_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Donation_hair_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Donation_hair_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Donation hair (cropped)","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"Robin Zebrowski","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Donation_hair_(cropped).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Donation_hair.jpg/960px-Donation_hair.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.