30 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Regarding Akuma's Form","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/regarding-akumas-form/150228","site":"T Nation · 95 posts · 2010"},{"title":"Shaved Head","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/shaved-head/155604","site":"T Nation · 83 posts · 2010"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Locks of Love - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locks_of_Love"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Hair (scalp)","chain":["Grow hair to donation length","Cut and donate","Fresh, shorter style"],"effect":"indirect","text":"The donor gets a planned cut and a visible style change; the charity receives hair for wigs."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Locks of Love-style hair donation is the practice of growing out hair and cutting it for donation to a charity that makes hairpieces for children with medical hair loss. For donors it doubles as a haircut project, ending in a shorter, lower-maintenance style.[1]","Locks of Love was founded on May 28, 1997 by Madonna Coffman, a nurse who had alopecia, and is based in West Palm Beach, Florida. It makes wigs for disadvantaged children up to age 21 affected by alopecia, burns or cancer treatment, and requires donated hair of at least 10 inches.[1]","Coverage in 2013 raised questions about hair valuations; Snopes attributed the figures to difficulty valuing hair. The charity said in 2007 that about 80 percent of donated hair was unsuitable for wigs and the rest was sold to fund its work.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Charity haircut"],["Founded","1997, Locks of Love[1]"],["Minimum length","10 inches[1]"],["Recipients","Children up to 21[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["Locks of Love was founded in 1997 and received IRS 501(c)(3) status in December 1997.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Controversies","paras":["In 2013 Forbes and the Huffington Post reported that up to $6 million of donated hair was unaccounted for yearly; Snopes attributed the discrepancy to valuation difficulty and found no black-market income in tax filings.[1] The IRS treats hair as a body part, so donating it is not tax-deductible, though the haircut cost may be.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]},{"h":"In forum culture","paras":["Forum users on T Nation occasionally mention growing hair to donate or shaving for a relative in treatment, usually as passing remarks."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1997","event":"Locks of Love founded in Florida.[1]"},{"year":"2007","event":"Charity says about 80 percent of donated hair is unsuitable for wigs.[1]"},{"year":"2013","event":"Media reports question hair valuations.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Locks of Love","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locks_of_Love","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"The Stupid Thread 2 (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-stupid-thread-2-part-1/219703","site":"T Nation · 9999 posts · 2016"},{"title":"Trump 2025 - Resuming The National Nightmare Of Peace And Prosperity (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/trump-2025-resuming-the-national-nightmare-of-peace-and-prosperity-part-1/289108","site":"T Nation · 9998 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Official 2021 T-ransformation Announcement Thread","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/official-2021-t-ransformation-announcement-thread/271058","site":"T Nation · 1537 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Atlas Shrugged; I Pressed","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/atlas-shrugged-i-pressed/177820","site":"T Nation · 1162 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Let's Process Our Feelings II","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/lets-process-our-feelings-ii/198052","site":"T Nation · 1140 posts · 2014"},{"title":"Ever Feel like a Threadkiller  45.0","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/ever-feel-like-a-threadkiller-45-0/167408","site":"T Nation · 1127 posts · 2011"}]}